-- lm = [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1], lmAnti = [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4], independent:
--   p((k, True))  = lm(k) * (1 - lmAnti(k))   = 0.36, 0.24, 0.14, 0.06 (sum 0.8)
--   p((k, False)) = lm(k) * lmAnti(k)         = 0.04, 0.06, 0.06, 0.04 (sum 0.2)
-- A token outside the domain has no mass either way. (A wildcard token,
-- (ANY, b), is a mask main is refused for, a separate gap.) The last block is
-- an anti-model certain of token 1: the veto of token 1 is exactly impossible
-- (the complement of a 1.0 read), every other token always passes.
p((0, True),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]))=(0.36, 0.0)
p((1, True),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]))=(0.24, 0.0)
p((2, True),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]))=(0.14, 0.0)
p((3, True),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]))=(0.06, 0.0)
p((0, False),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]))=(0.04, 0.0)
p((1, False),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]))=(0.06, 0.0)
p((2, False),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]))=(0.06, 0.0)
p((3, False),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]))=(0.04, 0.0)
p((2, ANY),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]))=(0.2, 0.0)
p((7, True),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4])) is impossible
p((-1, False),(2, [0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1]),(2, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4])) is impossible
